<code>assert \result != null && Arrays.equals(\result.toByteArray(), bytes);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.valueOf(bytes) != null && Arrays.equals(this.valueOf(bytes).toByteArray(), bytes);</code>

However, since the `valueOf` method returns a new `BitSet` instance and does not provide a direct method to retrieve the internal byte array, we need to rely on the `get` method to verify the bits. Here's a more accurate assertion based on the available methods:

<code>assert this.valueOf(bytes) != null && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < 8 * bytes.length; this.valueOf(bytes).get(i) == ((bytes[i / 8] & (1 << (i % 8))) != 0);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \result != null && Arrays.equals(\result.toByteArray(), bytes);</code>
--------------------
